{"name":"Lazy Afternoon","hex":"#97928b","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lazy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unwilling to do work or make an effort; disinclined to exertion.","Causing or characterised by idleness; relaxed or leisurely."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To laze, act in a lazy manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lazy"},{"term":"afternoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the day from noon or lunchtime until sunset, evening, or suppertime or 6pm.","The later part of anything, often with implications of decline."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the afternoon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afternoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lazy Afternoon (Barbra Streisand album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lazy Afternoon is the seventeenth studio album recorded by American singer Barbra Streisand. It was released on October 14, 1975, by Columbia Records. Following a mixed critical response to her previous studio album, ButterFly (1974), the singer began working with new musicians for the project. The album was recorded in April 1975 in Los Angeles. Producer Rupert Holmes wrote three songs on the album and co-wrote a fourth, \"By the Way\", with Streisand. She also included a few cover songs, such as the Four Tops' \"Shake Me, Wake Me \", Stevie Wonder's \"You and I\", and Libby Holman's \"Moanin' Low\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Barbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lazy_Afternoon_(Barbra_Streisand_album)"},{"title":"Afternoon","blocks":[{"text":"Afternoon is the period from noon to sunset or evening. It is the time when the sun is descending from its peak in the sky to somewhat before its terminus at the horizon in the west. In human life, it occupies roughly the latter half of the standard work and school day. In literal terms, it refers to a time specifically after noon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/330px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afternoon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Barbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg/250px-Barbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Barbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Barbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg/250px-Barbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarbra_Streisand_%E2%80%93_Lazy_Afternoon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/500px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/1280px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/500px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Türkenschanzpark in Vienna during the early afternoon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_(2376611600).jpg"},{"srcset":"https:/